1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1795 121 April 17 Ungk. Iver Bottolfsen Tøen 23 Amerika 1850 ( = Iver  BUTLER )
2 CONT
2 CONT ===History of Worth County (Publ. 1884) has a short informative biography on p.779 :===
2 CONT
2 CONT "Ivor BUTLER was born in Norway Feb.13, 1827. He emigrated to the United States, landing at Milwaukee Aug 5, 1850. He went to Walworth Co., Wis., and lived there for seven years; then moved to Kewaunee county, in same state, and f
2 CONC armed 14 years. 
2 CONT He married Caroline K. WIGEN Dec 26, 1857. She was a native of Norway. In 1869 they moved to Worth Co., Iowa where he is farming. He has 580 acres of land, and resides on section 5 in Kensett township. He is a thrifty, well to do 
2 CONC farmer, being largely engaged in stock. They have eleven children - Edward, Cornelius, Ole, Lewis, Bertinus, Charles, Alvin, Betsy, Sophia, Ellen and Julia. They are all members of the Norwegian Lutheran Church".
2 CONT
2 CONT 1880 cencus: farmer in Kensett, Worth, IA 
2 CONT
