1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1801 census for Hovde, Voss:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/ft/person/pf01058378000096<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''For Liland connections, consult Kindem’s Vossaboki IV, Bruk 1, page 543, following to page 549.'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 542.Skjelde/Liland<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Legends. People like to explain farm names. They tell that before anyone had settled in Viki, there was in Hardanger a man called Sjeldrup. One time one of his father’s cows got lost from the herd when they were up at the szeter. 
2 CONC Sjeldrup went looking for them. When he got over the mountain, he looked down into an exceedingly pleasant valley with a big lake. I’d like to live there, he thought. The mountain he called Graosio (Graside) after the bell cow tha
2 CONC t had strayed and was gray-colored. The next spring, Sjeldrup moved and settled in the valley he had seen and named the farm after himself: Sjelde. The oldest son, Grim built in an open area in the woods and called the farm Grimas
2 CONC tad. The next oldest son, Bjorn liked it near a birch glade (lund), built there and called the farm Lund. The third son Finn settled farther up. There was a lot of moss there, and he called the farm Mosaﬁnn. The youngest son Olav 
2 CONC got a lid (hillside) next to Skjelde and called it Liland. All the brothers agreed to build a pen for the sheep (saue) and called place Saude. Sjeldrup was buried where he had cleared and built.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''246. Liland.'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 543 Liland.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bruk 1.'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ……….<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 544 Liland.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Sjur Hovda owned 2 spann 14 mark in 1621……<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Brynjulv Jonson f. 1663 was the farmer in 1691 and 1701 and was g. m. Guro Andersdr.'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Tenant farmer Gunnar Flogo, in 1695, sued Brynjulv Liland for illegal ﬁshing in Flagaholen.<br/>
2 CONT During the case, it was discussed that '''Jon, Brynjulv’s father, had lived at Liland. It has been said that Brynjulv supposedly came from Afdal. Brynjulv died in 1723 and had the son Olav.''' At the estate settlement of Brynjulv 
2 CONC they owned 1‘/1 laup that was valued at 95 rd. '''Guro got married again in 1724 with Halldor Eirikson Afdal.'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Olav Brynjulvson f. 1710''' got in 1723 the deed for 1 laup 1 pund 18 mark and got '''married in 1736 with Brita Sjursdr. Vike. He died in 1774 and she in 1785, 69 1/2'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 545 Liland.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT years gl. They had '''three children: Anna f. 1739''', g. 1760 m. Knut Gusskalkson Eide, '''Guro f. 1745''', g. 1768 m. ekm. David Amundsen Rekve and '''Brynjulv f. 1750, g. 1776 m. Marta Torsteinsdr. Lunde.''' He was a grenadier 
2 CONC then. Brynjulv got in 1771, 1778 and 1786, the deed totaling 1 laup 1 pund 18 mark at Liland. '''Marta died in 1806 and Brynjulv in 1816. They had ten children: Brita f. 1777, g. 1797 m. Johannes Kolbeinson Hovda [see Hovda, Bruk 
2 CONC 1, p. 54].'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Olav f. 1778,'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Marta f. 1780, g. 1803 m. Nils Nilsson Nesthus, Guro f. in 1781, g.1. 1817 m. Gusskalk Eirikson Seim, 2. 1826 m. Magne Sjurson Skjeldal, cotter, Torstein f. 1783, g. 1819 m. the widow lngjerd Klasdr. Mosaﬁnn, lived at Seim, Guri f
2 CONC . 1787, g.1. 1813 m. Nils Eirikson Seim, Lars f. 1788, g. 1818 m. Anna Styrksdr. Seim, Knut f. 1790, g. 1822 m. Anna Larsdr. Skjelde, cotter, Sjur f. 1792, g.1. 1815 m. lngebjorg Klasdr. Mosaﬁnn, 2. 1867 m. Herborg Magnesdr. Kyte,
2 CONC  cotter at Mosaﬁnn and Anna f. 1797, g. 1816 m. Lars Andersson Skjelde. At the estate settlement of Brynjulv, the gross value Was 720 spd.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Olav Brynjulvson got married in 1816 m. Ingebjorg Andersdr. Skjelde''' and got the deed for the farm. He was mobilized in 1807 for the war against Sweden. Ingebjorg died in 1848, 53 years gl. and Olav in 1851. They had '''ﬁve c
2 CONC hildren: Marta f. 1817, g.'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 546 Liland.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1834 m. Olav Gusskalkson Eide f. 1804''', Steinvor f. 1818, g. 1845 m. Oleiv Knutson Grimastad, cotter at Narheim, Brita f. 1823, g. 1847 m. Nils Andersson Skjelde, '''Marta d. y. f. 1825, g. 1851 m. ekm. Olav Gusskalkson Eide'
2 CONC '', Guro f. 1828, g. 1854 m. Isak Larsson Skjelde, lived at Nedre Graudo.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Olav Gusskalkson got the deed from his father-in-law for the farm in 1834 and in 1849''' for 700 spd., each time half. Olav got '''ﬁve children with his first wife and six with the other:''' Margreta f. 1837, g. 1. 1857 m. Ande
2 CONC rs Larson Skjelde d. e., 2. 1861 m. Anders Larsson Skjelde d. y., '''Ingebjorg f. 1840, g. 1866 m. Velom Kolbeinson Hovda, [Velom, brother of Brynjolf Kolbeinson Hovde, got the Hovda farm].'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Gusskalk f. 1843, Anna f. 1845, g. 1871 m. Gusskalk Nilsson Flogo, Marta f. 1847, g. 1870 m. David Nilsson Vestrheim, Marta d. y. f. 1853, g. 1880 m. Arnﬁnn Masson Haga, Olav f. 1855, g. m. Brita Amundsdr. Nesheim, Vossastr., Kirs
2 CONC ti f. 1860, Brita f. 1862, g. 1892 m. shoemaker Knut Nilsson Skjelde, Brynjulv f. 1865 and Knut f. 1869 (America). Brynjulv was a peddler a while then went later to America. Olav Gusskalkson died in 1871 and Marta, his second wife
2 CONC , in 1892. At the estate settlement after Olav the farm was valued at 700 spd., and the gross value was 1420 spd.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Gusskalk Olavson got half of the farm in 1851 at the estate settlement after his father and the other half with the deed in 1872 from his mother. He was g. 1873 m. Anna Andersdr. Kvale. Gusskalk died in 1912 and Anna 1931. Their s
2 CONC on Anders got the farm in 1905 for 6,000 crowns. He was f. 1881 and g. m. Guri Kjelsdr. Nesheim, Vossestrand, f. 1882.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ……<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bruk 2.''' Liland. '''Set off from bruk 1 in 1890 with assessment 27 ore and sold to Brynjulv Olavson Liland who built a hotel. He sold it in 1893 to Olav, his brother, who later ran the hotel. Olav went peddling first, had lat
2 CONC er a general store in Strandebarm together with his cousin, Klas Olavson Liland. Thereafter, Olav ran the store in fishing season at Utsira until he bought the hotel. Olav is dead, and the son Sigurd, now has the hotel.'''<br/>
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 547-8 Liland.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Both in the 1700’s and until about in the 1880’s each year “strilers” (Bergen island people) came to Voss and bought timber. Usually the Ostrings were the lumberjacks in Bergen. At Voss, they were usually called “tymborstridla”. T
2 CONC hey went about the forests in the month of May and selected timber that then was hauled to the riverbanks, measured and paid about half of the purchase price. The seller watched for the spring ﬂood, then ﬂoated the timber ahead to
2 CONC  Lilandsosen (outlet of Lake Voss at Bulken). When the timbers from the various sellers had reached the outlet, usually at the end of June, the sellers and the buyers got together there. The timber was then delivered.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
