1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT http://look.no/anita/slekt/webcards/ps81/ps81_342.html
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/131284686/nils-aadson-sonve
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Nils Sonve is a perfect example of the typical Norwegian emigrant. He was born Nils Aadson, son of Aad/Odd Nielson Sonve and Guri Tormsdatter Gjelle in Voss, Hordaland, Norway. In america he used the name Nils Sonve in honor of th
2 CONC e farm he came from in Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Nels A. Sonve was born in Norway, July 24, 1831. Emigrating to America in 1869, he landed at Quebec. He went at once to McHenry Co., Ill., but only remained a short time. He then went to Wisconsin, staid five weeks and went to Min
2 CONC nesota. After remaining the winter, he went to Winneshiek Co., Iowa. He then went to Fillmore Co., Minn., .bought a farm and lived upon it three years. In 1874 he sold this and came to Worth county, where he purchased 160 acres on
2 CONC  section 11, Kensett township. He married Miss Tillong in 1854. She was born in Norway, in 1833. They have five childrenJulia, now Mrs. L. D. Klose; Christena, now Mrs. Spilde; Edward, Gilbert and Anna. They all belong to the Nor
2 CONC wegian Lutheran Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: History or Mitchell and Worth Counties, Iowa, 1883, Page 780.
