1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Baptism/birth record:
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QHV-13PP-1Z4N?i=32&cc=4237104&personaUrl=%2Fark%3A%2F61903%2F1%3A1%3A68QH-73YZ
2 CONT Index:
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:68QH-73YZ
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/31887991/randvie-knudsdatter-gilderhus
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Excerpts From Minnie Holtan's Memories==
2 CONT Grandmother was the only midwife for miles around and was often called away from home. Sometimes she’d stay many days if help was needed. If she had a baby herself, she had to take it with her, otherwise, she had to leave her own 
2 CONC children with my grandfather.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her pay for services rendered, I hear you say? Mostly calico for an apron, at the most enough cloth for a dress. Calico at that time was five cents a yard. 
2 CONT
2 CONT My memory of my grandmother was a crippled old lady–crippled from hard work and rheumatism. I never can remember her being able to walk alone. Two people had to help her. One held her under each arm. She was so bent over when she 
2 CONC sat on a chair that she had to have  strong piece of cloth tied to the back of the chair put under her arms and tied to the back of the chair with her feet on a box or she’d fall on her face. She was a little thin lady with lots o
2 CONC f pain. I really don’t know how many years she was in that condition. But hard work–carrying water in all kinds of weather–freezing, etc., everything put together was more than she could take, She lived as I can remember with her 
2 CONC daughter Anna. In the summertime she would come and live with my mother. Having only one downstairs bedroom which she needed, we couldn’t keep here in the winter time. Severt at that time worked in Kasson and often came to see her
2 CONC  and always gave her money for her own personal use. The only medicine I ever heard of her taking was Kuriko. I’m not so sure, but I think she died in February in 1900. I know we had to go in a sleigh to her funeral. Thus comes to
2 CONC  an end the lives of our hardworking and beloved grandparents.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://oiseth.org/Ole_and_Lena:_genealogy/?page_id=1136
