1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT The bygdebok does not make clear which Brita is Kolbein's mother.<br/>
2 CONT <br/>Note:  Gjertrud Johannesdr. f. 1758 was g. 1776 m. Kolbein Johannessen Berge and died in 1787. He was f. 1735 and died in 1785.  Please double-check Kolbein's death date.  Thanks. - Bob Hovde
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''For Berge/Hovde connections, consult Kindem’s Vossaboki II, Hovda, Bruk 1, page 54'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''54   Hovda.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bruk 1.'''  Hovda.  '''Johannes Steffason died 1761, 30 1/2 years g1., was g. m. Eli Larsdr. f. 1731 died 1794.''' He owned 1 laup after the deed transfer in 1754. '''Children: Gjertrud f. 1758''', Marta f 1760, g. 1782 m. Joha
2 CONC nnes Andersson Flogo. '''Gjertrud Johannesdr. f. 1758 was g. 1776 m. Kolbein Johannessen Berge and died in 1787. He was f. 1735 and died in 1785.''' He got in 1776 the deed on 1 laup which at the estate settlement after him was va
2 CONC lued at 280 rd. The gross value was 522 rd. '''Children: Johannes f. 1778, Brita f. 1776, g. 1803 m. David Nilsson Rekve.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johannes Kolbeinson f. 1778 was g. 1797 m. Brita Brynjulvsdr. Liland and died in 1876. She died in 1856, 77 1/2 years gl. He got his father’s farm. Children: Kolbein f. 1798''', Brynjulv f. 1799, g. 1828 m. widow Mari Gudleiksd
2 CONC r. Berge, America, Olav f. 1801, g. 1823 m. Kari Eiriksdr. Seim, settled in Manda]. Johannes f. 1809, ﬁrst a schoolmaster and later Sheriff at Evanger, g. 1. 1851 m. Herborg Olavsdr. Skiple, 2. 1857 m. Anna Nilsdr. Helland, Olav f
2 CONC . 1820, g. 1861 m. Marta Brynjulvsdr. Vaete, farmer at Vaete and he did a lot of brass work, Torstein f. 1822, storekeeper in Alesund, Gjertrud. 1803, g. 1821 m. Torgeir Larsson Seim, America, Marta f. 1806, g. 1842 m. Viking Viki
2 CONC ngson Repal, Anna f. 1811, g. 1840 m. Lars Gudleikson Hovda, Brita f. 1815, g. 1842 m. widower Knut Gusskalkson Eide.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Kolbein Johannessen f. 1798 was g. 1822 m. Sigvor Velomsdr. Berge and died in 1876. She was f. 1800 and died in 1892.''' He is recorded as a postal carrier when he was married and assumed the farm in 1828. Kolbein was his own c
2 CONC arpenter, blacksmith, shoemaker and tailor and worked at everything he.......... 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
