1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Josef was a superintendent, deputy elector, member of the district council, fire assessor and held other positions of trust. Josef made himself a wooden spoon machine which he powered with a water wheel. Both he an
2 CONC d his wife traveled to Chicago in 1890 to visit their children and relatives and stayed there for three years. Anna was born in 1819, died in 1903, and Josef died in 1909. Six daughters: Marta b. 1844, Ingjerd b. 1845, b. 1870 m. 
2 CONC Lars Josefson Lid, Guri b. 1847, b. 1871 m. Lars Jonson Bjørku, Kirsti b. 1850 (America), Sigvor b. 1858, married Olav Brynjulvson Glymme (America) and Soffi b. 1862, married Lars N. Hefte (America). Ho Marta in 1869 married Lars 
2 CONC Jonson Lid, born in 1841, and they got skates in 1878 from her father on the farm for 3,200 kronor. Lars died in 1887, and Marta left the farm to her sister Guri and her husband Lars Jonson Bjørku and traveled with her children to
2 CONC  America.
