1 NOTE (from Ættebok for Misjonsprest Anders Johanessen Rustad by Olav Rustad, 1948)  Anders emigrated in 1873 and first stayed in Jefferson Prairie, WI, but was in Koshkonong in 1874.  From there he moved to Vermillion, Dakota Territory
2 CONC , and for a time did farm-work.  For a year, around 1877, he was a seaman on the Missouri River from Yankton to Fort Benton and Fort Custer, and had some wild experiences in those days.  In the fall of 1878 he helped his brother K
2 CONC nut build at Lake Albert, Kingsbury County.  From there he went on foot 160 miles in 3 1/2 days and had meals only three times.  In the fall of 1879, he moved to Northwood, IA, and was there until 1897.  For 11 years, he was in a 
2 CONC flour mill (møllebruk for hvetemel) and for 6 years he had a store. ( After managing another flour mill at Nora Springs, Iowa for several years,) he returned to Kingsbury County in South Dakota and bought a farm which he worked un
2 CONC til 1916. Then he moved to Sioux Falls (SD).     Land records for the city of Northwood, Worth county, IA, show that Andrew bought and sold three pieces of property there.  The first was probably a business location, a half block 
2 CONC off Central (main) on 4th St. NW.  The legal description is Lot 3 of block 69.  He bought it for $310. July 25th, 1885, and sold it May 31st, 1902, after he moved to South Dakota.  The second property was a residence at 200 4th St
2 CONC , NW (Lot 10, Block 46).  He bought it for $100. August 18th, 1886, and sold it for $85. May 4th, 1891.  The third was a business location on Central, Lot 8 of Block 67.  He bought it for $570. on September 12th, 1890, and sold it
2 CONC  for $700. on July 6th, 1897.
