1 NOTE Mr. N. B. Anderson, for many years a resident of Northwood, died at the home of his son Joseph, in Sioux Falls, S. D. on Wednesday, March 14; his body was brought here by his sons and buried from Trinity church, Saturday last, Pas
2 CONC tor Siljan officiating.  Mr. Anderson was born in Voss, Norway, December 29, 1843. He came to America in 1872, and lived successively in Chicago, Sheridan, Ill., Slater, Story county, Iowa, Northwood, Emmons, and Sioux Falls.  By 
2 CONC far his longest stay in this country was made in Northwood which was his home from 1879 till some time in 1897 or 8, we think.  Mrs. Anderson died here is 1891, and their two daughters Sena and Celia, in 1893 and 1894 respectively
2 CONC . The other children, Martin and Joseph, who grew to young manhood here, are doing well in South Dakota.  The father, who had been in sadly failing health for a year and a half prior to his death, was cared for by those sons and b
2 CONC y them tenderly laid to rest with the loved one gone before.  Mr. Anderson was a man of large heart and much general intelligence, and for one whose opportunities had been so meagre a man of remarkably good ability.  His Northwood
2 CONC  friends were pleased to hear that he developed an unusual spirit of thoughtfulness and reverence during his last years.     To the Northwood friends who stood by us with loving helpfulness in the hour of our great need we wish he
2 CONC reby to express our sincerest thanks. Martin and Joseph Anderson.
