1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jackson, Minn., Nov, 8, 1930. Lars O. Teigen of Jackson, a member of the University of Minnesota board of regents and former member of the state legislature, died in a hospital here early today. He was 66 years old
2 CONC .  Mr Teigen, who had been in ill health for some time, suffered a paralytic stroke two weeks ago. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was appointed a member of the board of regents by the 1921 legislature. Prominent in the co-operative movement in this state, Mr Teigen helped organize the Jackson Farmers Elevator association and had been secretary since its f
2 CONC ormation 22 years ago. He served in the legislature several terms prior to four years ago.  In 1904, Mr Teigen introduced the bill which established the machinery factory at the state penitentiary.
