1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Princeton, Minn. Services will be held Sunday in Santiago, Minn., for Martin Teigen 81, former minister and state representative, who died here Wednesday Sep 2, 1953, after a heart attack.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr Teigen was a member of the University of Minnesota football team for three years in the mid 1890s.  He graduated from Luther seminary, St Paul, in 1900 and served in the Lutheran ministry until 1913, when he resigned because of
2 CONC  ill health (Mastoiditis).  He was elected as representative to the state legislature from Mille Lacs county in 1931 and 1933.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT University of Minnesota Alumni Weekly, Nov 9, 1914, History of Football at Minnesota:  
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin Teigen, Newburg, Bottineau Co., North Dakota, Born at Medo, Blue Earth Co., Minnesota; Norwegian ancestry; m. Mathilda Wollan, December 16, 1905; three boys, 7, 5, 3 and one girl 9 months; entered the University of Minnesot
2 CONC a as a special student from Luther College, Decatur, Iowa; graduated from Lutheran seminary in 1900; tackle in 1895, half-back in 1896; Lutheran pastor, has organized and served twenty on the frontiers of North Dakota, serving as 
2 CONC many as fifteen congregations at the one time for three years; for the past two years has been living on his farm on account of his health; candidate for state representative at the fall election.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Marriage license Nov 1905, Ward County, ND. Rev. Martin Teigen, 33, Bottineau, ND, Mathilda Wollan, 27, Pope, Minn. Married Dec 16, 1905. First Lutheran, Minot, North Dakota. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Oct 1915, he became the manager and grain buyer at the Farmers Elevator in Kramer, ND.
