3 ADR1 Fyre
3 STAE Hordaland
3 CTRY Norge
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =The Origin of the Fyre / Fyhre / Føre / Førde Last Name=
2 CONT It seems that the last name Fyre comes from the name of the farm that Ole Sjurson's brother https://www.geni.com/people/Anders-Sjurson/6000000003875696296 purchased in 1800, which later passed to him (see source below).  Since Ole
2 CONC  Sjurson's children have birth records showing a last name starting with an F all with different spellings, it is likely that all of these are related to the Fyre name: Fond, Førde, Førd, and Føre.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ole Sjurson's record in FamilySearch.org has the following comment (in Norwegian) posted by user ctbergesen2768253:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ole fikk gården Fyhre i 1809 etter moren Ingeborg, mot å forsørge henne. Moren, Ingeborg, fikk i 1808 gården Fyhre av sø nnen Anders som døde ugift i 1808. Anders kjøpte gården av Nils Hachorson i 1800. Skifte i 1798 fikk kreditor
2 CONC en Nils Hac horson gården fra Sjur Pederson Bjørndalen. Sjur fikk gården i 1795 i makeskifte av Gulleik Larsson. Før dette bodde de på Bj 3 CONT ørndalen gård.
2 CONT
2 CONT Google translates this as:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ole got the farm Fyhre in 1809 after his mother Ingeborg [https://www.geni.com/people/Ingebj%C3%B8rg-Gavle/6000000003875680758], in exchange for supporting her. In 1808, the mother, Ingeborg, received the farm Fyhre from her son A
2 CONC nders [https://www.geni.com/people/Anders-Sjurson/6000000003875696296], who died unmarried in 1808. Anders had bought the farm from Nils Hachorson in 1800. In 1798, the creditor Nils Hachorson received the farm from Sjur Pederson 
2 CONC Bjørndalen. Sjur got the farm in 1795 in a change of spouse from Gulleik Larsson. Before this they lived at Bj 3 CONT ørndalen farm.
