1 NAME Johannes Styrkson /Rue/
2 GIVN Johannes Styrkson
2 SURN Rue
2 _MARNM Rue
2 NICK Rue ?
1 NAME Johannes Styrksson //
2 GIVN Johannes Styrksson
2 SURN Berge
2 NICK Rue ?
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1692
2 PLAC Rue, Voss, Hordaland, Norway
2 ADDR
1 BURI
2 DATE 1743
2 PLAC Voss, Hordaland, Norway
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1743
2 PLAC Berge, Voss, Hordaland, Norway
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Rue (Giljane)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Probable reference to Johannes Styrkson (Rue) is found in Kindem's Vossaboki IV, Rue (Giljane), page 384,  as follows:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes Styrkson leased in 1727 1/2 laup from Henrik Miltzow.  He deeded 1/2 laup 6 mark in 1728 to Rognald Arnbjørnson for 120 rd.  He bought the redemption rights to 1/2 laup in 1760 for 122 rd. that G. Marselis (in) had  owned
2 CONC  in his time.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''For overview of Johannes Styrkson Rue and Brita Kolbeinsdatter Tveite, consult Kindem’s Vossaboki II, Berge, pages 63-72 and Lyngvær’s Voss Bygdebok, ÆTTEBOK for Vossestrand, Tveite Hb, page 200.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Berge.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 63-68 Berge.<br/>
2 CONT <br/>In 1730, '''Johannes Styrkson''' and Johannes Larsson are listed as owner and operators. The latter was from Gjerde and exchanged in 1729 with Erling Rognaldson for 2 laup in Berge. Johannes was a grandson (son’s son) of Joha
2 CONC nnes  Sverkveson Seve, who was married with the ﬁrst wife of Sheriff Mass Seve. Johannes Larsson who died in 1778, 80 years g1., was g. m. Steinvor Kolbeinsdr. dead 1752, 51 years g1. and had six children. He sold the farm in 1748
2 CONC  to Arnved Jonson Skjerve. Continued bruk 1.<br/>
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johannes Styrkson Rue''' was g. 1. m. Brita Styrksdr., '''2. m. Brita Kolbeinsdr., who died in 1783, 87 years gl. In 1727, he bought 2 laup in Berge. At his estate settlement in 1743 are listed six children: Styrk, Eiliv, Kolbe
2 CONC in, Hallstein, Synneva and Brita.'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Styrk was g. 1746 m. widow Barbra Jakobsdr. Lisseim.'''  [See Lisseim, Bruk 1, pages 60-61, in Kindem.]<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Kolbein f. 1736 married in 1765 m. Kari Knutsdr. Lunde.  Hallstein'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 69 Berge.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''f. 1730 was g. 1766 m. Kari Andersdr. Lisseim.''' Brita married in 1750 m. Per Olavson Lisseim. '''Eiliv was f. 1728, died in 1802, and was g. 1753 m. Sigvor Velomsdr. Eide.''' They had '''10 children'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eiliv, in 1757, got the deed from his siblings for 2 pund 8 mark, in 1773, the deed from his mother for 1 laup, bought from Hallstein Lisseim, his brother, in 1773, 6 mark in Ovre-Berge, and bought the redemption rights for 2 laup
2 CONC   in Berge in 1760 for 33 rd. 66 skill. Gabriel Marselis had bought the property in 1657. In 1783, Eiliv leased to his oldest son, Johannes, 1 laup and in 1788 to his son Velom 1 laup.
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes f. 1755, died in 1810, and was g. 1783 m. ek. Marta Ivarsdr. Bo. They didn’t have children. He leased the farm to '''Velom, his brother'''. He also leased l laup again in 1798 to his brother-in-law, Kolbein Person Gavle. 
2 CONC  Continued at bruk 4.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition, Velom bought in 1798 from his father 12 mark in Ovre-Berge. '''Velom f. 1759, died in 1810, was g. 1798 m. Kari Olavsdr. Tesdal,''' dead 1808. In 1804, he was before the court for having struck Mattis Mousson Berge wi
2 CONC th a grain pole, so he died about a month later. Velom was sentenced to “work in irons” for 5 years at Bergenhus fortress. He also was to pay a compensation judgment and court costs. Continued at bruk 5.<br/>
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ''The individual bruks.''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Bruk l. Berge. '''Arnved Jonson Skjerve had as above stated bought 2 laup in Berge in 1748.''' It became bruk 1. 9 mark belongs to the bruk, which the Vangs church owned.  '''Arnved was the second husband of the sheriff daughter S
2 CONC ofﬁ Massdr. Seve.'''  Arnved got 1760 a royal deed and redemption rights to 2 laup in Berge for 33 rd. 66 skill. Gabriel Marselis had bought the property in 1657. '''Arnved and Sofﬁ had the daughters Marta, Brita, Sofﬁ'''<br/>
2 CONT ....<br/>
2 CONT Bruk 2. Berge. As previously mentioned Sjur Josefson became the owner ofl laup in this bruk in 1796. Vang’s Church owned 41/2 mark. Sjur traded 1800 with Kolbein Person for 1 pund in Gavle. Kolbein '''sold the farm again in 1816 t
2 CONC o Olav Andersson Vaete. He was, in 1805, g. m. Brita Eilivsdr. Berge, sister of Kolbein’s wife and daughter of the previously mentioned Eiliv Johannessen.'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 71-75 Berge.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Bruks 3, 4.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Bruk 5. Berge. Above is told that Velom Eilivson was owner of this bruk. He had only his daughter Sigvor f. 1800 and leased the farm in 1811 to Styrk, his brother….<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT sold it again in 1865 to Olav Johannessen Hovda for 550 spd. His widow, Malta Brynjulvsdr., was g. m. Svein Andersson Kvale, who got the deed on the farm in 1874.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Summary from Lyngvær, page 200.'''<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Kolbein Olson ytre Sundve (1668-1733) married Marta Halsteisdatter and had two daughters, Brita (1695) who in 1719 married Johannes Styrkson Rue and Steinvor (1701) who in 1725 married Johannes Larsson ø.Vinje.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
