1 NOTE Lars, born on Haukenes, had the following sponsors, according to the records from the Hadsel Parish; Johannes Olson Vasvig, Hans Hartvigsen Bredvig, Ole Knudson Grytting, Breda Olsdtr. Haukenes, and Lise Petersdtr. Holmsnes (wife 
2 CONC of Bård Knutson).     Lars and Syneva moved directly to Freeborn County, MN, in 1869-70 where there were several others who had come from Vik i Sogn.  Many were also from the Tryti farm that was Syneva's family's place of origin. 
2 CONC  Sponsors of their children born in Bath Township were often names found in the "EIN STAD SKAL EIN VERA" (1989 history of emigration from Vik which lists Lars' family leaving).
2 CONT      Lars and his family are listed in the 1870, 1875, and 1880 census records of Bath Township. The 1880 census includes Lars, Sonneva, Martin O., Knut, Albert, Josephine O., Gilbert, Anton, Eduard, and 4 month old Louise. The fi
2 CONC rst two children were born in Norway, and Albert through Louise are listed in Freeborn County or parish records as born in Bath Township.  Sponsors were found on microfilm of "Freeborn Parish, 1865-1888" (March 29, 1990, Jean Legr
2 CONC ied, Oakland, MN)  Papers for the naturalization of Lewis Knudson Sofjord (signed in his handwriting as Lars Knudson Sofjord) were filed December 15, 1875 at Albert Lea.  They indicate he arrived in Detroit in June of 1869.
2 CONT      (From records at Albert Lea, Freeborn County, MN, March 6, 1991) Lewis Knutson Sofjord bought 80 acres in Bath township, Freeborn County, MN (section 31, the north half of the SW quarter) from Alexander Smith for $1375 in Apr
2 CONC il of 1875.  He evidently paid $415 and had a mortgage for the remaining $960. In December of 1879 after Alexander died, his wife Rachel filed papers against Lewis Knutson Sofjord and his wife Sonneva Knutson Sofjord - perhaps the
2 CONC y were behind in payments.  Lars and Syneva moved by covered wagon to North Dakota in 1881.  Lind township was organized in the fall of 1881 at Lars' sod house, named after John Lindstrom.  In Bath township, Lars lived about 4 mil
2 CONC es south of his younger brother, John.  Bath township is about 10 miles north of Albert Lea, Minnesota.     In North Dakota, record of birth and confirmation of John's children were in the book for Claremont Church, found at the N
2 CONC orthwood Evangelical Lutheran Church.
