1 NOTE According to Arthur Markve records, Martha's farm name was Gjørsten, which must have been Gjøstein.  She is not to be found in the Vossestrand book on the Vinje farm, a name sometimes associated with her.  From the Rene book, page
2 CONC  781 has a person that could be her nephew with the Leidal name.  "Anders Knutson Leidal, carpenter and house owner in Chicago was born on the Leidal farm at Voss on the 4th of April 1868 of parents Knut Larson Gjøstein, born 1829
2 CONC  and died 1909, and wife Guro Johannesdtr. Leidal, born 1832 and died 1885, farmers on Leidal."
2 CONT
2 CONT The church records of Voss list among those leaving for north Norway, Bridta Larsdatter Vinje, age 16, leaving April 4th, 1842.  She was unmarried and was with a person ervidently her sister, Andri Larsdatter Vinje, age 19.  Desti
2 CONC nation was Kobbervig.  As Nils and Martha were married in 1849, this could be the correct Martha.
