1 NOTE (translated from Norwegian in the Rene Book by RAF, p477) Ole emigrated in 1856 to America with his wife, Ingeborg, and their two children, Knut and Anna.  After a nine weeks journey across the ocean, they arrived in Quebec and we
2 CONC nt further to York, Green county, WI., where the first stayed with Erik Meland.  Ole got work with a farmer in the area and earned 50 cents a day.  In 1859 the bought 40 acres of forested land in the south east corner of Perry tow
2 CONC nship and he built an earth house for his family.  They lived in it until 1867 when he built a better house.
