1 NOTE Bystølen, Høn, Nesheim, Hagahaugen, Tveite HB and Fliseram were farm names that were the last part of the name as Norwegians moved from farm to farm. Nils Persson Fliseram lived on Bystølen when he was married.  In 1867, he bought
2 CONC  the Fliseram farm and moved there in 1873.  Andrew was the first of the family to be born there; the others were born on Bystølen. Fliseram was a larger farm earlier and in 1806 was divided into Fliseram, Bygd and Oppheim.  Micro
2 CONC film records of the census dated December 31, 1865 show living on Bystølen were: Nils Person, farmer, 36; Gjøri, wife, 37; Synneva, daughter, 8; Peder, son 5; Viking, son, 1; (and parents) Per Nilson, 66; Ingri Persdtr., 76.
